# Home Base

Generic control plane: systemd **`homebased`**, binary **`homebase`**. Production port from **`HOMEBASE_PORT`** in `.env` (default **8080**, systemd as root). Dev API **:8081**, Next **:3081** (proxies `/api` + `/ws`) — can run beside prod. Projects come from gitignored `config/projects.json`.

## Hard rules

- Never expose PTY/shell/process/file APIs without a valid session JWT (`Authorization: Bearer` or `?token=`).
- Auth is **password → JWT (24h TTL)**. Password is scrypt-hashed in `.runtime/auth.json` (mode 0600). Only a **localhost-loaded** SPA may set/change the password.
- Share QR issues a **one-time redeem id** (20s), never the password or a long-lived secret; redeem returns a normal 24h JWT.
- Never commit `.env`, `config/projects.json`, `.runtime/`, or personal presets under `config/presets/` (only `example.json` is committed).
- Cursor integration: **local** `cursor-sdk` agents only. Chat agents get Home Base identity context and in-process `homebase_*` custom tools (not a public HTTP MCP).
- View (remote screen) is JWT-gated like PTY; capture must stop when no subscribers remain (Vision agent hold may keep the worker warm while Armed).
- Vision desktop control (Linux X11) requires an explicit Arm; never expose pointer/keyboard tools without JWT + Arm.
- Actions are config-driven (button → script + args). Do not hardcode project names or paths into the server.
- Scripts must resolve inside the project directory.
- Notification history is capped; prefer pagination over loading all rows into memory.
- Auth lockout: after 5 failures escalate delays to a full day; log failures daily under `.runtime/logs/`.
- Client API/WS must stay same-origin relative paths (`/api`, `/ws`) — no hardcoded host/port in the SPA.
- Always bump the repo `VERSION` file (semver patch by default; minor/major when the change warrants it) whenever you make code or behavior changes. Do this in the same turn as the change — before finishing.
- **Chat durability:** workspaces under `.runtime/chats/` must flush mid-stream (debounced) and on SIGTERM/SIGINT so `--deploy` does not drop assistant/tool history. Only delete a chat when the user deletes that tab.
- **UI areas:** post-login **Home** dashboard → **Agent** · **Homework** · **Home Access** · **Vision** (X11 desktop + chat). See `home-access.mdc` / `vision.mdc`.
- **Cursor API key:** prefer in-app encrypted vault (`.runtime/cursor_api_key.enc`); env `CURSOR_API_KEY` is an override only.
- **First install:** `./build.sh --onboarding` (or `--setup`) seeds this repo as the `homebase` project. Apps **+** / `homebase_project_upsert` add more.

## Entry points

- `./build.sh --onboarding` (setup + seed + deploy on Linux) / `--setup` / `--clean` / `--run` / `--add-project --preset …`
- Backend: Bun `server/src/entry.ts`
- Frontend: Next.js static export `web/` → `web/dist` (brotli/gzip siblings)
- Deploy: `./build.sh --deploy` → Bun compile → `/usr/share/homebased` + wrapper + systemd (Linux only)
